{%- comment -%}
  PG R36S Mobile: on phones, one photo and the orb page's running order.

  Registered in templates/product.pg-landing.json only (the R36S), and every
  rule is ≤900px — desktop keeps the full gallery and the column it has today.

  ONE PICTURE. pg-landing's gallery column renders .pgx-hero (the first image),
  .pgx-vid (the clip from the section's "Gallery video URL" setting) and
  .pgx-thumbwrap (every other image). Per the owner the phone should open on the
  Pokémon R36S shot alone, so the clip and the strip are hidden and the hero —
  which IS that shot, media[0] on the product — is what is left.

  The strip is hidden in two places on purpose. pg-landing sets
  `.pgx-thumbwrap{display:contents}` under 900px, which makes the wrapper vanish
  as a box and promotes .pgx-thumbs to be the gallery's own child, so hiding the
  wrapper alone does nothing there; pg-gallery-mobile then re-asserts the
  wrapper as a real block. Hiding the wrapper AND the strip covers both states.
  Nothing is deleted — the images stay on the product and desktop still shows
  the carousel.

  THE SAME RUNNING ORDER AS THE ORB. The orb page gets its phone layout from
  pg-tiktok-pdp, which turns .pgx-buy into a flex column and sets an explicit
  order on each child, so the page reads: title, stars, BUNDLE & SAVE, the
  tiles, add to cart, the sellout-risk card, then the review carousel, then the
  info row, payment icons, guarantee and accordions.

  The R36S had pg-landing's plain DOM order instead — the review carousel sat
  directly under the stars, above the bundle, and the sellout card above that.
  The same order values are restated here so the two pages read identically:

      title 1 | rating 2 | divider 3 | tiles 4 | deal note + ATC 5
      sellout slot 6 (from pg-sellout-last) | err 6 | quote 8
      sellout 9 (only if the slot has not claimed it yet) | info 10
      payment 11 | guarantee 12 | accordions 13

  Order is set rather than nodes moved for the same reason pg-tiktok-pdp does
  it: pg-mobile's quoteUp() re-seats the review card after the rating every
  1.5s, and several other scripts insert relative to their siblings, so any DOM
  move would be fought. Nothing here moves a node.

  pg-sellout-last (also registered on this template) is what puts the sellout
  card under the last bundle tile; this file only gives its wrapper the seat.

  AN ADD TO CART IN EVERY TILE, like the orb. pg-tiktok-pdp puts one inside each
  ladder tile on the orb, shown only while that tile is selected, and hides the
  big bottom button on phones so there is exactly one button on screen and it
  belongs to the offer being looked at. The R36S has no ladder — its tiles are
  pg-landing's own Single Item and Bundle Deal 2x — so the same treatment is
  rebuilt here against those, with pg-tiktok-pdp's styling restated because that
  file does not render on this template.

  It is a SPAN with role=button, not a <button>: the base theme paints buttons
  with a dark ::before overlay. It does not carry .pgx-atc either, since
  pg-landing binds its add-to-cart to #pgx-atc by id and a second element with
  that class would only confuse anything looking for "the" button. A click
  clicks #pgx-atc instead, so pg-landing's own handler posts the selected tile's
  variants unaided — a programmatic .click() works on a display:none element,
  which is what lets the bottom button be hidden while still doing the work. The
  click also bubbles to the tile, whose own handler selects it, so the tile a
  shopper buys from is always the tile they pressed.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  @media (max-width:900px){
    /* ---- one picture: no clip, no filmstrip ---- */
    #pgx .pgx-vid{display:none !important}
    #pgx .pgx-thumbwrap{display:none !important}
    #pgx .pgx-thumbs{display:none !important}
    #pgx .pgx-tharrow{display:none !important}

    /* ---- the orb page's running order ---- */
    #pgx .pgx-buy{display:flex;flex-direction:column}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > *{order:7}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-title{order:1}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-rating{order:2}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-bs{order:3}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-divider{order:3}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-tile{order:4}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-deal-note{order:5}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-atc{order:5}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-err{order:6}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-quote{order:8;margin-top:16px}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-sellout{order:9}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-info{order:10}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pg-payrow{order:11}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-pay{order:11}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-guar{order:12}
    #pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-acc{order:13}

    /* ---- an ADD TO CART inside the selected tile ---- */
    #pgx .pgx-tile.pgx-sel .pg-r36-atc{
      display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;
      margin-top:12px;padding:15px 12px;
      border-radius:10px;
      background:linear-gradient(120deg,#9B4BC4 0%,#7A2FA2 55%,#5E2380 100%);
      color:#FFFFFF;
      font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
      font-size:15.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;
      text-align:center;cursor:pointer;
      box-shadow:0 14px 30px -12px rgba(139,68,190,.75);
      -webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;
      transition:filter .15s ease,opacity .15s ease;
    }
    #pgx .pgx-tile.pgx-sel .pg-r36-atc:hover{filter:brightness(1.1)}
    #pgx .pgx-tile.pgx-sel .pg-r36-atc.busy{opacity:.6;cursor:default}
    #pgx .pgx-tile.pgx-sel .pg-r36-atc:after{content:"\2192";font-size:17px;line-height:1}
    /* the bottom button would duplicate the in-tile one on phones. Browsers
       without :has() simply keep both, which is harmless. */
    #pgx .pgx-buy:has(.pgx-tile .pg-r36-atc) > .pgx-atc{display:none !important}
  }
  /* hidden by default and at every width, so an unselected tile never shows one
     and desktop never shows any */
  #pgx .pgx-tile .pg-r36-atc{display:none}
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgR36Atc) return; window.pgR36Atc = 1;

  function buttons(){
    document.querySelectorAll('#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-tile[data-pgx-tile]').forEach(function(tile){
      if (tile.querySelector('.pg-r36-atc')) return;
      var b = document.createElement('span');
      b.className = 'pg-r36-atc';
      b.setAttribute('role', 'button');
      b.setAttribute('tabindex', '0');
      b.textContent = 'Add to cart';
      b.addEventListener('click', function(){
        if (b.classList.contains('busy')) return;
        var atc = document.getElementById('pgx-atc');
        if (!atc) return;
        b.classList.add('busy');
        b.textContent = 'Adding…';
        /* pg-landing's own handler reads the selected tile and posts it */
        atc.click();
        setTimeout(function(){ b.classList.remove('busy'); b.textContent = 'Add to cart'; }, 2600);
      });
      b.addEventListener('keydown', function(e){
        if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' '){ e.preventDefault(); b.click(); }
      });
      tile.appendChild(b);
    });
  }

  function boot(){
    buttons();
    var root = document.getElementById('pgx');
    if (root && window.MutationObserver){
      var q = false;
      new MutationObserver(function(){
        if (q) return;
        q = true;
        setTimeout(function(){ q = false; buttons(); }, 80);
      }).observe(root, {childList: true, subtree: true});
    }
    setInterval(buttons, 900);
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot); else boot();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG R36S Mobile", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG R36S Mobile"}]}
{% endschema %}
